/* llms BYTEADD / ALUADD (apply_byteadd.py, 11-03 14:2x): two in-level heat probes, off unless set (instruments, never shipped). LLMS_DS4_BYTEADD=<MiB a step> (ALT 'byteadd'): a command buffer of its own, committed from the step hook before the step's work, streams that many MiB from a 256-MiB private buffer (float4 loads summed, a never-true store) -- DRAM traffic at near-zero ALU. LLMS_DS4_ALUADD=<iterations> (ALT 'aluadd'): the same placement, a register-only float4 FMA chain -- GPU heat, no DRAM bytes. Each sums its buffers' GPU time (timestamps) and prints the mean at exit: a level's Walsh contrast minus that direct time is the slowdown the probe's heat adds to the rest of the step. */

